### Key Observations

**This is a regrade, and the delta checks out.** The draft first scored C (7.5) with Evidence capped at 6 and Discoverability at 6. Uncapping those two mechanically accounts for ~1.3 of the 1.4-point jump — so the movement is the revision pass doing its job, not me re-scoring the prose more generously. The other four dimensions landed where the first grade had them, except Hook (I read it a point higher).

**What the revision actually fixed.** It pulled the real NYT Popcast transcript and pinned every floating childhood quote to it, sourced the father's trial to Bunnie XO's *Dumb Blonde* (Aug 2024), and ran the frontmatter enrich stage. Source audit now returns 6 inline / 1 vague / **0 untagged**. All five FAQ anchors resolve to real headings (verified).

**The standout.** Rebuilding the Type 3 tiebreaker on the December 2023 blackout tattoo after the unverifiable therapy quote was killed produced a *better* argument than the one it replaced: he paid for 78 hours of pain to erase the visual identity that made him famous, and left one line showing. That's a signature detail in the rubric's exact sense.

**What holds it at B+.** Writing, and only Writing. Five sections close on the same short aphoristic reframe, plus three reader-command imperatives against 0–1 in each of the three most recently graded drafts. The full pipeline architecture is visible at every joint, which the 9-band explicitly excludes. The Eminem section also still reads as the SEO obligation it is — it names the honest gap and then resolves it biographically, so the type never explains anything there.

**Sameness cap did not fire.** Checked against Penguinz0, KSI, Brooke-Monk. It shares the epigraph→cold-open furniture (structural, exempt) but notably *avoids* the "What would change our mind:" counterargument closer all three recent drafts use near-verbatim. The same-type similarity trip at 0.084 vs megan-fox is a genuine false positive on the token "New York Times" — the ledger's call to keep the attribution is right.

**One flag for whoever revises:** the Razzie claim ("seven nominations and handed him Worst Director") carries no year or awarding body, and I could not independently verify the nomination count. It's load-bearing for the Good Mourning beat, which is the piece's second critic-pressure anchor.

Frontmatter written to the draft; feedback sidecar at `docs/content-analysis/grades/Machine-Gun-Kelly.review.md`. No legacy `QUALITY GRADE` block was present to remove.

